cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite Burn Clock and the upstream datasets when using this software.
  The collective author is provisional; no Burn Clock DOI has been assigned.
  Code is MIT licensed. The derived data compilation is CC BY 4.0, subject to
  the source rights and attribution described in DATA_LICENSE.md.
type: software
title: "Burn Clock: satellite timing and fire activity"
authors:
  - name: "Burn Clock contributors"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
url: "https://burn-clock.ottoskibeli.chatgpt.site/"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Awsomni5s/burn-clock"
abstract: >-
  An application for examining satellite observation times, harmonized fire
  activity calendars, and the Punjab afternoon burning comparison. Historical
  observations end in December 2025. Satellite detections, active cell-days,
  and geostationary pixel-hours are distinct measures; none is a direct measure
  of emissions or burned area. The supplied scientific pipeline has not been
  fully rerun during the application build.
keywords:
  - active fire
  - satellite observation timing
  - MODIS
  - VIIRS
  - GK2A
references:
  - type: data
    title: "Hourly Fire Detection Dataset of Post-monsoon Stubble Burning in Northwestern India derived from GK2-AMI Geostationary Satellite Observations"
    authors:
      - family-names: Jethva
        given-names: Hiren
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20084790"
    version: "v1"
    date-released: "2026-05-12"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    url: "https://zenodo.org/records/20084790"
  - type: data
    title: "Fire Information for Resource Management System (FIRMS)"
    authors:
      - name: "NASA FIRMS"
    url: "https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/"
